Peacefulls are herdable to some extent.  They won't walk into you
and that eliminates 1 of the 8 directions.  For the ones that don't
dig they also won't go through walls and that further narrows down
their movement options.

Going down through minetown I often use this trick to herd the
watch into rooms once I have a key.  They will open doors but they
do not have keys and will not break down doors to get out.  It takes
some patience but I'll got around opening every door on the level,
then herd all of the watch into rooms and lock the doors.  I end up
with several closed and locked rooms.  By the time I come back up
and it becomes likely that digging dwarfs will dig through the walls
I have gained the strength to kill them one by one if I chose to.

A similar strategy should work somewhat for peacefull diggers.
It may be very inefficient but it's better than completely random
movement.  Or just spend so much time on the level that they dig
the area with their random movement or until one of the digging
dwarves dies from a trap.

